[COLOR dodgerblue][B]Version 0.2.11[/B][/COLOR]
- Fixed a native Kodi crash that could happen when returning to the Home screen after adding, removing, or editing list items (or marking watched).
- In-plugin list edits now reliably refresh both the open list and its matching Home widget once you settle back on Home.
- "Refresh Widgets" context-menu item is now a single entry per list (dropped the redundant duplicate).
- "Show Notification after Refresh" setting is now always configurable (previously hidden unless the periodic refresh timer was set).


[COLOR dodgerblue][B]Version 0.2.10[/B][/COLOR]
- Mixed Providers and Mixed Genres widgets now honor "sort_by=random": add &sort_by=random to the widget path to shuffle the displayed titles (matches Mixed Channels).


[COLOR dodgerblue][B]Version 0.2.9[/B][/COLOR]
- New "Mixed My Lists" folder under Mixed Movies & TV: blended movie + TV views of your own lists — Trakt Collection/Watchlist and TMDb Watchlist/Favorites/Recommendations.
- Provider menus (Movies, TV Shows, and Mixed Providers) now fold each brand's per-storefront duplicates into one entry, so picking e.g. "Starz" searches all its channels instead of just one.
- Mixed Providers list cleaned up: deduplicated, sorted alphabetically, with crisper local brand icons.
- Mixed Channels widgets now honor a "sort_by=random" path, shuffling the rendered page.


[COLOR dodgerblue][B]Version 0.2.8[/B][/COLOR]
- New: Forge can now be used as a player for TMDBHelper — play movies and episodes from TMDBHelper widgets/lists through Forge instead of seeing "Playback through external addons is not supported".
- Added Tools > "Install TMDBHelper Player": one tap copies the Forge player configs into TMDBHelper, adding "Forge - Auto Play" and "Forge - Source Select" to its "Play with..." menu (restart Kodi afterward).


[COLOR dodgerblue][B]Version 0.2.7[/B][/COLOR]
- New "Skip Intro/Outro" feature: a Netflix-style Skip button appears during episode playback to jump past intros, recaps, and outros.
- Skip timings come from crowd-sourced IntroDB data, with AniSkip used for anime episodes and an optional chapter-based fallback.
- Configure under Settings > Playback: enable it, toggle AniSkip, and tune minimum confidence/submissions and button duration (off by default).
- Skip-marker data is cached and can be cleared from the maintenance menu ("Clear Skip Markers Cache").
- Stability fix: reworked the "In Progress" home widget to reduce a thread race that could crash Kodi.


[COLOR dodgerblue][B]Version 0.2.6[/B][/COLOR]
- New "Quick Add" context-menu item: one tap adds or removes the highlighted movie/show from a single chosen list.
- Pick your Quick Add target in Settings > Context Menu: Trakt Watchlist, TMDb Watchlist/Favorites, Forge Favorites, or any of your Trakt/TMDb/Forge personal lists.
- The menu entry reads "Add to ..." or "Remove from ..." depending on whether the item is already in that list.
- When no target is set, it falls back to your Trakt Watchlist (or Forge Favorites if Trakt isn't connected).


